<div class="not-content">
  <section class="home-reference" aria-label="Why Artifacts">
    <div><h2>Files become part of your product.</h2><p>A generated report needs its inputs. An approved document needs a saved version. A worker needs access to its workspace. As these files change, your app needs history, consistent versions, and a way to share the work.</p><p>Artifacts provides repositories for those files through an API. You can create a workspace, publish related changes together, and retrieve the exact result later.</p></div>
    <div class="model-note"><h2>Your app owns the workflow.</h2><p>Keep users, job status, search, and business records in your application. Store the versioned inputs and outputs in Artifacts, and save their repository address and commit SHA with your record.</p><a href="/artifacts/core/concepts/">Understand the model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-paths" aria-labelledby="start-building">
    <div class="home-section-heading"><h2>From the first file to your app.</h2></div>
    <div class="learning-paths">
      <a class="path-card" href="/artifacts/core/concepts/"><strong>Files and their history</strong><p>Follow a report through revisions. Learn when to use a repository, a commit, and a branch.</p><span class="path-cta">Explore the concepts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      <a class="path-card" href="/artifacts/getting-started/"><strong>Your first repository</strong><p>Write files through REST, update them with Git, and read the same history through either interface.</p><span class="path-cta">Follow the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      <a class="path-card" href="/artifacts/core/integration/"><strong>Connect it to your app</strong><p>Choose a repository boundary, save the result with your application record, and add a worker when needed.</p><span class="path-cta">Build an integration <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-reference" aria-label="Keep building">
    <div><h2>See it in an application</h2><p>A repository can last for one job or grow with a project. The same primitives support generated reports, agent sessions, and personal memory.</p><div class="reference-links"><a href="/artifacts/examples/">Application examples <span>Explore the patterns ↗</span></a></div></div>
